{
  "contract": "KRI-1138 slide tilt v1. Canvas = the slide OUTPUT canvas in px (origin top-left, y down). The MEDIA is the photo's (cropped) region scaled the way the slide frames it, cover scale (max) for Fill and whole-photo scale (min) for Fit, centred on the canvas; for Fill it is larger than the canvas on one axis. rotation_deg is clockwise-positive about the CANVAS centre (y down: x' = cx + dx*cos - dy*sin, y' = cy + dx*sin + dy*cos), in -180..180; 0 is upright and stored as no tilt. expected.corners are the media's top-left, top-right, bottom-right, bottom-left after the turn; rotated_bounds is the axis-aligned box of the turned media (ffmpeg rotw/roth); covers_canvas is true when the turned media still covers every canvas pixel (no backdrop shows). Only the media turns: text, ink, stickers and the watermark stay upright above it. Tolerance 1e-6. 'validation' lists tilt values with the expected verdict; for invalid cases 'reason' is a keyword the server error message contains. backdrop kinds: blank (black), color (#RRGGBB, required for color and refused for the others), blur (blurred cover-fit copy of the same media, sigma FIT_BLUR_SIGMA_PX = 80 at full resolution).",
  "version": 1,
  "caps": {
    "rotation_deg_min": -180,
    "rotation_deg_max": 180,
    "blur_sigma_px": 80
  },
